          "height": 380,
          "content": "Section / Header (reusable, id G0wNOc) — slot signature:\n\n• logo-slot (id adoph) — slot:[] (untyped, Plan 25-03 may retroactively type), enabled:true. Default content: 'Crito' wordmark text placeholder (DM Sans 36/700, navy). Consumers override at instance time with Joel-brand wordmark or custom logo node.\n\n• nav-links (id wvv1T) — fixed text nodes (6) lifted from Crito source per D-38. Literal labels: Home, Pages, Pricing, Portfolio, Blog, Contact (Inter 16/500, navy). Per-instance label overrides happen via descendants in Phase 31 Homepage instance time (Joel's actual nav: Blog, Projects, FAQ, Contact).\n\n• cta-row (id yVNDw) — horizontal frame containing 1 Button ref instance (B1 user gate strict source-wins: Crito Menu bar source shows 1 CTA, not 2). Primary instance (ciMov) ref M7eUr with label 'Get Started Free' override and iconTrailing slot wired with lucide arrow-right per D-44 — resolves OPEN-24-06 via actual production use.\n\nNot shipped (A1 user gate strict source-wins resolution): Crito Menu bar affordances row (search / chevron-down / hamburger icons). The earlier PEN-INVENTORY Phase 24 Icon-Glyphs 'Menu bar' attribution was factually incorrect — those glyphs live elsewhere in ujMLJ. The 3 glyphs themselves stay in Phase 24 ship-set for Phase 26+ consumers.\n\nAll children use Pencil auto-layout (LAYOUT-01). Component width 1200 fixed per D-41 matching Crito Menu bar effective visual.\n\nSee 25-01-SUMMARY.md and PEN-INVENTORY § Variant Evidence (Phase 24) Phase-25-late-additions for full audit trail."
