        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "x48zh",
          "name": "Section / Footer — slot signature",
          "width": 1200,
          "height": 480,
          "content": "Section / Footer (reusable, id Xs0Hs) — slot signature:\n\n• logo-slot (id kkO4M, inside brand-column) — slot:[] (untyped), enabled:true. Default: 'Crito' wordmark text placeholder (DM Sans 36/700, navy). Consumers override at instance time with Joel-brand wordmark.\n\n• brand-column tagline (id uubl4) — fixed text, Crito source literal per D-48 ('Phasellus pulvinar...'). Phase 31 instance overrides with Joel's actual tagline.\n\n• brand-column social-row (id B9gNb) — ships JOEL-BRAND defaults at component level per Pitfall 7: Instagram (lucide Pattern A) + Substack (Pattern B atomic-glyph AzmgQ from simpleicons canonical SVG). Crito's Twitter + LinkedIn NOT shipped — Joel uses Instagram + Substack.\n\n• link-columns (id NO9J5) — 3 columns matching Crito source `iHrsm` audit: Useful Links / Help & Support / Resources. Each: Chivo 16/700 navy heading + 4 Chivo 16/normal links (Crito source literals per D-48). Phase 31 instance overrides labels with Joel's actual nav set.\n\n• copyright-row (id l4jp3) — right-aligned copyright text, Chivo 14/normal opacity 0.8. Crito source literal '© 2024 Crito. All Right Reserved'.\n\nNot shipped from Crito source: Mobile + Email contact rows (Joel has contact info elsewhere); 2 raster-baked image buttons (Pitfall 7 — not reconstructable). These deferred to a future Joel-Footer-content phase if needed.\n\nAll typography uses Chivo per D-47 (Phase 23's conditional Chivo primitive type-primitive-family-chivo earns its keep). Footer bg #fafafaff binds to color-semantic-bg-surface per Crito source audit.\n\nSee 25-02-SUMMARY.md and PEN-INVENTORY § Variant Evidence + § Glyphs Shipped (Phase 25) for full audit trail."
        },
